---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
const updated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10);
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Shameel | DevOps in Progress" description="Privacy policy for shameel.barchy.online — what contact data is collected, how it’s used, and your rights. Resend-only, no database retention.">
  <main class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-20 py-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{label:"Home", href:"/"}, {label:"Privacy Policy"}]} />
      <div class="mt-8">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-pastel-blue/40 border border-blue-200/40 text-xs font-semibold text-blue-700">Privacy Policy</span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-fg mt-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-fg-faint mt-2">Last updated: {updated} · shameel.barchy.online</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 prose prose-sm max-w-none prose-headings:text-fg prose-headings:font-bold prose-p:text-fg-muted prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-a:text-accent prose-strong:text-fg prose-li:text-fg-muted bg-white rounded-2xl border border-border p-6 md:p-8">
        <p>This is a personal portfolio. I take your data seriously even though I collect very little.</p>

        <h2>What I collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact form</strong>: name, email, and message you submit at <code>/#contact</code>. Sent via <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Resend</a> to <code>muhammadshameelks@gmail.com</code>. <strong>No database</strong> — I don’t store submissions in PocketBase, Convex, or any DB. Email only.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics</strong>: <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> — privacy-first, no cookies, no personal data, no cross-site tracking. Used only to see which pages are visited.</li>
          <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: Cloudflare may log IP and user-agent for rate-limiting (5 messages / 15 min per IP) and abuse prevention. Logs are not used for tracking.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What I don’t collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No accounts, no passwords, no payment data.</li>
          <li>No ad trackers, no Facebook Pixel, no GA4.</li>
          <li>No selling or sharing your contact data with third parties.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How I use contact data</h2>
        <p>Only to reply to you. I reply within 12 hours (usually same day). I keep the email thread in my Gmail so I can follow up — you can ask me to delete it at any time.</p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>Email-only: the message is forwarded to my Gmail and not stored elsewhere. If I add a lightweight store later (e.g., Cloudflare D1 for a dashboard), this policy will be updated with retention period and you’ll see the change date above.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:muhammadshameelks@gmail.com">muhammadshameelks@gmail.com</a> to request access, correction, or deletion of any message you sent. I’ll confirm within 12 hours.</p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>This site does not set cookies except strictly necessary ones from Cloudflare for security. No cookie banner is needed for the current setup. If that changes, a banner will appear.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Data controller: Muhammad Shameel KS, Palakkad, Kerala, India — <a href="mailto:muhammadshameelks@gmail.com">muhammadshameelks@gmail.com</a>.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>I’ll update this page when the contact backend or analytics changes. The date at the top always reflects the latest version.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 text-xs text-fg-faint">
        Maps adaptation: I’m based in Palakkad, Kerala and work remote worldwide. No street address is shared. See contact card on the <a href="/#contact" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent">homepage</a>.
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
